+# Agent Note: Checked Session Model Migration
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-10-checked-session-model-migration.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+An existing session may exceed another model's context allowance. A reasoning gateway can also require plaintext reasoning alongside historical tool calls, even though ordinary cross-provider replay discards native reasoning state.
+
+## Decision
+
+Checked selection is opt-in and commits only after idle-state and event-revision checks around a destination capability snapshot. The existing token meter reprices retained work, including the latest request overhead. The destination replaces adapter-owned output defaults, while explicit caps remain user choices. Successful selection uses the existing durable session event without saving a deployment default.
+
+The pi-ai provider option enables a gateway-specific request projection. Foreign plaintext reasoning uses pi-ai's JSON replay carrier for a fresh reasoning item; it does not forge a provider signature. Foreign calls receive consistent request-local IDs, and their results follow those IDs. Native route metadata is retained only on its originating route. Stored events remain the source record.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+Automatic compaction can discard work and needs its own user policy; this operation refuses and lets callers compact or select a larger destination. Globally converting reasoning would send a gateway extension to providers that do not support it. Reusing foreign signatures would mistake opaque provider state for portable text.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Admission is an estimate of current work, with no reservation for later input and no external availability guarantee. Empty sessions still require declared capacity. Legacy selection behavior remains available. The [model picker decision](2026-07-24-web-session-model-selector.md) and [wire compatibility decision](2026-08-18-pi-ai-wire-compat-surface.md) remain active: this opt-in extension does not replace their ordinary selection or compatibility rules.
+
+## Testing
+
+A keyless recorded HTTP exchange drives the real Loader, agent loop, session controller, token meter, and tools. Reopening retained events preserves the new route; failed admission preserves the original route. The request snapshot pins the plaintext gateway representation. Exact-capacity, output-default, stale-session, and foreign replay cases verify admission and serialization separately.
+
+Admission distinguishes caller allowance, adapter request default, and model output capability. Both window and capability must be known. The model-selection event carries caller allowance even without a request header, so an empty session retains that choice after reopening. A catalog-only capability reserves space without becoming a caller setting.
+
+Chat reasoning-only assistant messages retain their position through SDK conversion using a request-local marker removed by the payload callback. The gateway receives the original plaintext reasoning with null content, never marker text. This compensates for the pinned SDK dropping messages without visible content or calls; same-route replay remains owned by the SDK.
